  "Question": "Jones covered a distance of \\(50\\) miles on his first trip. On a later trip he traveled \\(300\\) miles while going three times as fast. His new time compared with the old time was:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "three times as much",
    "B": "twice as much",
    "C": "the same",
    "D": "half as much",
    "E": "a third as much"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Travel time equals distance divided by speed. The new distance is \\(300/50=6\\) times the old distance, which would require six times the time at the old speed. Traveling three times as fast divides that time by three, so\n\\[\n\\frac{\\text{new time}}{\\text{old time}}=\\frac{6}{3}=2.\n\\]\nThe new time was twice as much, choice B.",
